{title: Thank God For The Blood}
{key: Bb}
{x_theme: salvation, blood, faith-trust, grace-mercy}
{x_source: chrd:thank_god_for_the_blood.chrd}

{comment: Verse 1}
[Bb]In sin I wandered sore and sad
With a [F]bleeding heart and [Bb]aching head,
Till [Bb]Jesus [Dm]came and [Gm]sweetly [Bb]said,
I'll [F]take thy [Bb/D]sins    [F/C]a   -   [Bb]way.

{comment: Chorus}
[Bb]Thank God for the blood!
Thank [F]God for the [Bb]blood!
Thank God for the [Gm]blood
That [F]washes [Bb/D]white   [F/C]as      [Bb]snow.

{comment: Verse 2}
[Bb]I gave my heart, my life, my all
To [F]Him who drank the [Bb]cup of gall
To [Bb]raise the [Dm]guilty [Gm]from the [Bb]fall
And t[F]ake their [Bb/D]sins    [F/C]a   -   [Bb]way.

{comment: Verse 3}
[Bb]The water, Spirit and the blood
A[F]gree, if we but [Bb]understood,
In [Bb]making [Dm]sinners [Gm]pure and [Bb]good,
And t[F]ake their [Bb/D]sins    [F/C]a   -   [Bb]way.

{comment: Verse 4}
[Bb]How wonderful God's mighty plan!
How [F]grace the awful [Bb]guilt did span
When [Bb]He took [Dm]on the [Gm]form of [Bb]man
To [F]take our [Bb/D]sins    [F/C]a   -   [Bb]way.

{comment: Verse 5}
[Bb]We cannot know, we may not tell
How [F]we are saved from [Bb]death and hell;
Thru [Bb]faith we [Dm]know that [Gm]all is [Bb]well
He [F]took our [Bb/D]sins    [F/C]a   -   [Bb]way.
